            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The partition rule gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(B)&=P(A\\cap B)+P(\\overline A\\cap B)\\\\P(B)&=P(A)P(B\\mid A)+P(\\overline A)P(B\\mid\\overline A).\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute this expression into Bayes’ theorem:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{P(A)P(B\\mid A)}{P(B)}\\\\P(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{P(A)P(B\\mid A)}{P(A)P(B\\mid A)+P(\\overline A)P(B\\mid\\overline A)}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
